# CAMEL OVERKILL: SPITTOON. Sits between the nav terminal and the ballast pumps.
name camel_ballast
box battery
note "SPITTOON: HOW IT WORKS" "Normally passes the nav terminal's depth signal straight to the ballast pumps (a relay, on).\nType 'spit' in CamelOS (bus 7300): for 10 s the relay blocks the pilot and a signal check sends -100 (empty the tanks): the camel spits its ballast and rises. Good for a flooded front ballast tank or a dramatic exit.\nThen control returns to the pilot."
note "WIRING" "in1 <- nav terminal velocity_y_out\nout1 -> set_targetlevel of the ballast pumps"
c rx wifi Channel=7300
c sp regex Expression="^(?i)spit$" Output=1 FalseOutput="" ContinuousOutput=false
c hold or TimeFrame=10
c ns not
c gate relay IsOn=true
c blow check TargetSignal=1 Output=-100 FalseOutput=""
w rx.out sp.in
w sp.out hold.1
w hold.out ns.in blow.in
w ns.out gate.set_state
w in1 gate.1
w gate.signal_out1 out1
w blow.out out1
